AccountV3Security (internal stateful candidate, NOT Account/4337/factory)
├── given a policy seeded ONLY by the test harness
│   ├── when preparing security/bootstrap
│   │   ├── require account/generation/version/predecessor/window/scope/current nonce
│   │   ├── require OLD authority and new/changed descriptor possession
│   │   ├── accept only a five-minute consent; sign a distinct bounded proposal deadline
│   │   ├── after acceptance expiry, require fresh commit; preserve veto and exact proposal expiry
│   │   ├── consume admin nonce; store pending; leave old policy and version intact
│   │   └── commit with separate fresh OLD authority; replace all members; advance manifest once
│   ├── when preparing recovery
│   │   ├── require recovery authority, not admin signatures
│   │   ├── replace pending admin, never another recovery
│   │   ├── wait from acceptance using OLD delay, never validAfter or new delay
│   │   ├── block spend guard even after expiry until explicit cleanup
│   │   └── anyone activates at readyAt before expiry, without asset or proxy effects
│   ├── when vetoing
│   │   ├── current member can veto with its independent nonce
│   │   └── removed/new member, stale/replayed/purpose-substituted signatures fail
│   ├── when expiring
│   │   └── anyone clears exactly the expired proposal, never its consumed nonces
│   ├── when freezing upgrades
│   │   ├── fresh admin authority irreversibly freezes; no policy/version change
│   │   └── preserves pending recovery; clears seeded upgrade but does NOT prove upgrade execution
│   └── when reentrant/uninitialized/overflow/corrupted/stale
│       └── fail closed with unchanged security state
└── stateful randomized sequences with real signatures
    ├── versions count exactly installed policies; predecessor and policy remain consistent
    ├── admin/recovery/veto nonces equal accepted actions and never roll back on cancellation
    ├── only authorized pending proposals exist; freeze is monotonic
    ├── pending recovery can never pass spendEnabled or commitPolicy
    └── ETH/ERC20/proxy slot are unchanged by all security transitions
